	(text "Input: SK810L crowbar (a reversed pigtail clamps at about 1 V; U7 on the main board limits and times out), 1 uF at the connector, 2.2 uH filter, 47 uF aluminium (0.42 Ohm\nESR damps the filter and the pigtail), 5 x 2.2 uF hot-loop ceramics at Q1. tools/absorber_sim.py (main board) runs the bank-trip spike through U7, F2, the pigtail and\nthis filter.\nUVLO: 300k / 12.4k: on at 30.2 V, off at 27.2 V (10 uA hysteresis current). Below the 30.5 V worst sag at 90 A from a 38 V pack, so motor load can't brown out compute\nbefore the BMS does; the Pi still shuts down on its load-aware threshold.\nON/OFF: the main board's 2N7002 pulls pin 5 low through 220R when U7's PGD is good. Pin 5 open: 220k from VIN biases the NPN, which holds EN low (off). Pin 5 low: NPN\noff, EN rises: on. Pin 5 idles at about 2.7 V, like the DVE's.\nPower train (TI design 2 uprated): 400 kHz (RT 24.9k), 6.8 uH 8.9 mOhm 21.8 A Isat, 3.3 A ripple; Q1 BSC070N10NS5 (low Qgd), Q2 BSC040N10NS5. Valley limit by Q2 RDS(on):\n200 uA x 402R / 4.5 mOhm = 18 A cold, about 12-13 A hot: over the 11.6 A ceiling, under the 19-21 A of the inductor. Hiccup on overload.\nOutput: 12.0 V (0.8 V x (1 + 21k / 1.5k)), 5 x 22 uF here, plus 330 uF + 2 x 22 uF on the main board at the far end of the pigtail. Compensation is TI's for this L and C\n(40 kHz crossover). The pigtail and 330 uF resonate near 20 kHz: measure the loop with an injection resistor in place of the 0R before trusting it. VCC from VOUT through\nBAT46W (TI's D1) cuts bias loss.\nLoss at 12 A, 48 V (est): Q1 0.4 W conduction + 1.2 W switching, Q2 0.7 W, inductor 1.3 W, controller 0.3 W: about 4 W, 97 %. Board: 2 layers, 2 oz, about 45 x 35 mm,\nbolted to the rail with a thermal pad like the DVE."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
